From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] Make FIOM writable with supervisor mode
Purpose: Preserves privileged-ISA FIOM CSR semantics in the embedded Spike hart.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

FIOM may be read-only zero when satp.MODE is always Bare, but need not be.
Expose it in both machine and supervisor environment configuration CSR masks
whenever supervisor mode is implemented, including Bare-only harts.

diff --git a/riscv/csr_init.cc b/riscv/csr_init.cc
index 58658ad5..2856688c 100644
--- a/riscv/csr_init.cc
+++ b/riscv/csr_init.cc
@@ -236,9 +236,8 @@ void state_t::csr_init(processor_t* const proc, reg_t max_isa)
     add_hypervisor_csr(CSR_HIDELEG, hideleg);
   }
 
-  // The spec allows FIOM to read as zero only where there is no S-mode or no
-  // paging, so it is writable exactly when neither holds.
-  const bool fiom_writable = proc->extension_enabled('S') && proc->get_max_vaddr_bits() > 0;
+  // This embedded hart keeps FIOM writable with S-mode, including Bare-only harts.
+  const bool fiom_writable = proc->extension_enabled('S');
   const reg_t menvcfg_mask = (fiom_writable ? MENVCFG_FIOM : 0) |
                             (proc->extension_enabled(EXT_ZICBOM) ? MENVCFG_CBCFE | MENVCFG_CBIE : 0) |
                             (proc->extension_enabled(EXT_ZICBOZ) ? MENVCFG_CBZE : 0) |
